course: dictionary
lesson: 7486
title: Possessive words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Possessive is a word with two everyday meanings and one grammar meaning. A person can be possessive: they want to keep someone or something all to themselves. «My best friend gets possessive if I play with someone else.» Here it means they do not like to share you.
explain: In grammar, a possessive word shows that something belongs to someone. «My», «your», «his», «her», «our», «their» and «its» are possessive words. A name with an apostrophe and s, like «Sam's», is possessive too.
explain: Look for the thing that is owned. In «my bike», my shows who owns the bike, and bike is the noun it belongs to. Before a noun these words are called possessive determiners. Mine and yours standing alone are possessive pronouns.
fact: Possessive means showing that something belongs to someone.
fact: The possessive apostrophe in «the dog's bone» shows one dog owns the bone.
fact: «My», «your», «his», «her», «our» and «their» before a noun are called possessive determiners.
fact: A possessive friend or dog wants to keep someone or something to itself and does not like sharing.
fact: «Its» is possessive and has no apostrophe; «it's» means «it is».
exercise: «My bag is heavy.» Which word in this sentence is possessive? | *My | is | bag | heavy
exercise: A friend who wants you all to herself is being possessive. What does that mean? | Happy to share everything | Very tall | *Not wanting to share | Always late
exercise: In «the dog's bone», what does the apostrophe s show? | A missing letter only | *That one dog owns the bone | A question is being asked | More than one dog
test: «Their house is near the park.» Which word is a possessive determiner? | Park | House | *Their | Near
test: «The cat licked ___ paw.» Choose the possessive word that shows the paw belongs to the cat. | it's | itself | it | *its
exam: «The bike is ___.» Which possessive pronoun standing alone fills the gap? | my | me | I | *mine
